From: ZJJCKA <96774959+ZJJCKA@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: modpost: silence missing module description warnings

OpenWrt builds MediaTek with CONFIG_MODULE_STRIPPED=y, which deliberately
removes non-essential description metadata from kernel modules.  Linux 6.18
still warns for every resulting module object, producing a large amount of
build-log noise even though the module code and required metadata are valid.

Drop only the MODULE_DESCRIPTION warning.  License checks, unresolved symbol
checks, namespace checks, section mismatch checks and every other modpost
diagnostic remain unchanged.

---
 scripts/mod/modpost.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

--- a/scripts/mod/modpost.c
+++ b/scripts/mod/modpost.c
@@ -1611,10 +1611,6 @@ static void read_symbols(const char *mod
 			add_namespace(&mod->imported_namespaces, namespace);
 		}
 
-#ifndef CONFIG_MODULE_STRIPPED
-		if (!get_modinfo(&info, "description"))
-			warn("missing MODULE_DESCRIPTION() in %s\n", modname);
-#endif
 	}
 
 	for (sym = info.symtab_start; sym < info.symtab_stop; sym++) {
